WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.263 --> 00:00:02.389
HAPPENING THERE RIGHT NOW.

00:00:02.423 --> 00:00:04.243
&gt;&gt; Bill: ISSUES GALOR.

00:00:04.277 --> 00:00:05.558
ONE BORDER TOWN.

00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:07.617
25% OF MIGRANTS DROPPED OFF AT

00:00:07.618 --> 00:00:08.669
A SHELTER TESTED POSITIVE FOR

00:00:08.671 --> 00:00:09.096
COVID.

00:00:09.098 --> 00:00:11.195
THE DIRECTOR SAYS IT WAS JUST

00:00:11.197 --> 00:00:13.697
IN THE FIRST GROUP DROPPED OFF.

00:00:13.698 --> 00:00:16.153
THE ACTUAL NUMBER MAY GO HIGHER

00:00:16.188 --> 00:00:17.819
HAPPENING IN HARLINGEN, TEXAS.

00:00:17.853 --> 00:00:19.243
THE MAYOR, CHRIS BOSWELL.

00:00:19.245 --> 00:00:20.822
WHITE HOUSE DOESN’T SAY IT’S A

00:00:20.823 --> 00:00:21.356
CRISIS.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.663
THEY’RE ASKING FOR VOLUNTEERS

00:00:22.664 --> 00:00:23.473
TO HELP.

00:00:23.474 --> 00:00:26.043
IF IT’S NOT A CRISIS, WHY DO

00:00:26.077 --> 00:00:27.565
YOU NEED VOLUNTEERS AND HOW

00:00:27.566 --> 00:00:28.362
WOULD YOU CHARACTERIZE IT,

00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:29.538
MAYOR?

00:00:29.539 --> 00:00:33.108
&gt;&gt; GOOD MORNING, THANK YOU FOR

00:00:33.109 --> 00:00:35.378
HAVING ME ON.

00:00:35.379 --> 00:00:37.394
CERTAINLY CAN TURN INTO A

00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:38.359
HUMANITARIAN CRISIS.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.629
WE’VE SEEN THIS BEFORE A FEW

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:42.069
YEARS AGO.

00:00:42.071 --> 00:00:44.681
WHEN THE UNACCOMPANIED MINORS

00:00:44.682 --> 00:00:46.704
IN PARTICULAR COME TO OUR

00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:48.143
COMMUNITIES, THEY DON’T HAVE

00:00:48.177 --> 00:00:49.107
ANYPLACE TO GO.

00:00:49.108 --> 00:00:51.493
ALTHOUGH WE HAVE SHELTERS THAT

00:00:51.494 --> 00:00:53.260
HAVE BEEN OPERATING IN OUR

00:00:53.295 --> 00:00:54.432
COMMUNITIES, INCLUDING

00:00:54.466 --> 00:00:56.586
HARLINGEN FOR A NUMBER OF YEARS.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:59.372
TRADITIONAL SHELTERS OPERATE

00:00:59.407 --> 00:01:01.814
WELL AND SAFELY FOR THE

00:01:01.815 --> 00:01:02.717
UNACCOMPANIED MINORS.

00:01:02.718 --> 00:01:04.709
WHEN THERE IS SUCH AN INFLUX IT

00:01:04.743 --> 00:01:06.183
CAN BE A DANGEROUS SITUATION.

00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:07.317
&gt;&gt; Dana: WHAT’S THE IMPACT ON

00:01:07.318 --> 00:01:08.552
YOUR TOWN?

00:01:08.553 --> 00:01:11.067
I THINK LOCAL GOVERNMENT IS THE

00:01:11.068 --> 00:01:12.194
ACTUALLY THE HARDEST GOVERNMENT

00:01:12.196 --> 00:01:13.565
WHERE YOU ACTUALLY HAVE TO DO

00:01:13.566 --> 00:01:15.171
THINGS FOR PEOPLE.

00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:17.154
WHAT’S THE IMPACT FOR YOU?

00:01:17.155 --> 00:01:19.216
&gt;&gt; WELL, THESE ARE DECISIONS

00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:21.091
MADE BY THE FEDERAL GOVERNMENT

00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:24.562
AND SHOULD BE HANDLED BY THE

00:01:24.564 --> 00:01:26.650
FEDERAL GOVERNMENT BUT THEY

00:01:26.651 --> 00:01:28.573
TURN INTO PROBLEMS FOR LOCAL

00:01:28.608 --> 00:01:31.109
GOVERNMENTS BECAUSE ABOUT THREE

00:01:31.143 --> 00:01:33.221
WEEKS AGO THE BORDER PATROL

00:01:33.223 --> 00:01:35.238
TOLD US IN McALLEN, BROWNSVILLE

00:01:35.272 --> 00:01:37.464
AND HARLINGEN THEY WOULD BE

00:01:37.498 --> 00:01:39.055
RELEASING PRIMARILY FAMILIES

00:01:39.056 --> 00:01:40.012
INTO OUR COMMUNITIES.

00:01:40.047 --> 00:01:42.888
THEY COME HERE NOT -- THIS IS

00:01:42.922 --> 00:01:43.858
NOT THE ENDPOINT.

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:45.507
THIS IS NOT THEIR FINAL

00:01:45.509 --> 00:01:46.219
DESTINATION.

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.787
THEY’RE BEING RELEASED INTO

00:01:47.788 --> 00:01:48.921
BROWNSVILLE, McALLEN AND

00:01:48.922 --> 00:01:51.357
HARLINGEN BECAUSE WE HAVE

00:01:51.358 --> 00:01:53.121
AIRPORTS AND BUS STATIONS AND

00:01:53.156 --> 00:01:54.423
CHARITY FACILITIES.

00:01:54.457 --> 00:01:56.778
AND SO WHEN THOSE CHARITY

00:01:56.813 --> 00:01:58.616
FACILITIES CAN’T ACCOMMODATE

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.715
THEM, THEN WE HAVE TO PROVIDE

00:02:01.749 --> 00:02:03.037
ADDITIONAL ACCOMMODATIONS FOR

00:02:03.071 --> 00:02:03.913
THEM.

00:02:03.914 --> 00:02:08.872
SO WE HAVE -- OUR CITY COUNCIL

00:02:08.874 --> 00:02:11.988
HAS OPENED UP ONE OF OUR

00:02:11.989 --> 00:02:13.851
FACILITIES, COMMUNITY CENTER,

00:02:13.852 --> 00:02:15.686
IN CASE OUR LOCAL CHARITY

00:02:15.687 --> 00:02:16.868
LOAVES AND FISHES NEEDS THAT

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.879
ADDITIONAL SPACE.

00:02:17.914 --> 00:02:20.573
SO THAT BECOMES A BURDEN AND AN

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:21.646
EXPENSE ON THE LOCAL

00:02:21.647 --> 00:02:21.923
GOVERNMENTS.

00:02:21.924 --> 00:02:23.502
OUR LOCAL GOVERNMENTS REALLY

00:02:23.537 --> 00:02:25.611
NEED TO HAVE HELP FROM THE

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.008
FEDERAL GOVERNMENT TO RESPOND

00:02:27.043 --> 00:02:28.228
TO THE RELEASE OF THESE

00:02:28.263 --> 00:02:29.842
IMMIGRANTS INTO OUR COMMUNITIES.

00:02:29.876 --> 00:02:33.909
&gt;&gt; Bill: IT IS MARCH 9th.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:38.255
DID YOU SEE THIS COMING?

00:02:38.256 --> 00:02:40.638
&gt;&gt; WELL, OBVIOUSLY WITH THE

00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:42.497
ELECTION THERE WERE THE IDEA

00:02:42.498 --> 00:02:44.023
THAT THERE WOULD BE A CHANGE IN

00:02:44.024 --> 00:02:44.444
POLICY.

00:02:44.478 --> 00:02:46.244
WE KNEW THERE WOULD BE A CHANGE

00:02:46.278 --> 00:02:48.449
IN POLICY.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.235
WE ALSO KNEW THERE WERE LARGE

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:55.804
NUMBERS OF IMMIGRANTS CAMPED IN

00:02:55.805 --> 00:02:58.255
MEXICO WAITING TO BE -- TO

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.818
ENTER THE UNITED STATES TO SEEK

00:02:59.852 --> 00:03:00.617
ASYLUM.

00:03:00.652 --> 00:03:03.319
SO ONCE THE POLICY CHANGED,

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.921
THEN SURE, THEY ARE GOING TO

00:03:05.922 --> 00:03:08.264
MOVE ACROSS AND THEN TRY TO

00:03:08.299 --> 00:03:09.434
FIND THEIR FINAL DESTINATIONS.

00:03:09.436 --> 00:03:11.623
ONE OF THE THINGS ABOUT -- THIS

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.895
IS NOT JUST A BORDER ISSUE.

00:03:14.929 --> 00:03:17.076
THIS IS AN ISSUE FOR EVERYONE

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.070
BECAUSE THESE FOLKS AS I SAID,

00:03:19.105 --> 00:03:22.295
THIS IS NOT THEIR FINAL

00:03:22.296 --> 00:03:24.978
DESTINATION ALONG THE BORDER.

00:03:25.011 --> 00:03:30.281
&gt;&gt; Bill: ONE MORE PRECISE

00:03:30.316 --> 00:03:31.157
QUESTION.

00:03:31.158 --> 00:03:34.243
JEN PSAKI SAID WE’RE HERE IN

00:03:34.278 --> 00:03:35.465
THIS CIRCUMSTANCE BECAUSE WE’RE

00:03:35.499 --> 00:03:37.006
HUMANE.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.339
WAS THE LAST ADMINISTRATION

00:03:40.373 --> 00:03:41.152
INHUMANE?

00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:45.138
&gt;&gt; WELL, MANY OF US BELIEVE

00:03:45.172 --> 00:03:48.458
THAT IT IS NOT HUMANE TO HAVE

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:50.761
YOUNG CHILDREN TRAVEL FROM

00:03:50.762 --> 00:03:53.355
CENTRAL AMERICA TO THE BORDER

00:03:53.356 --> 00:03:58.374
AND THAT IS NOT -- THAT IS

00:03:58.375 --> 00:03:59.997
FRAUGHT WITH POTENTIAL PROBLEMS

00:03:59.998 --> 00:04:01.429
OF TRAFFICKING AND DIFFICULTIES

00:04:01.463 --> 00:04:04.840
IN TRAVELING SO FAR FOR SUCH A

00:04:04.841 --> 00:04:06.979
LONG PERIOD OF TIME.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:09.109
AND I THINK THERE HAS BEEN IN

00:04:09.144 --> 00:04:10.696
THE PAST BIPARTISAN CONCERNS

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.265
ABOUT THAT BEING A HUMANITARIAN

00:04:13.299 --> 00:04:13.621
PROBLEM.

00:04:13.655 --> 00:04:15.214
&gt;&gt; Dana: MR. MAYOR, THANK YOU

00:04:15.216 --> 00:04:15.691
SO MUCH FOR BEING WITH US TODAY

